WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.400
You're here.
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.133
It's going to be fun tonight.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.434
Well, let's get
to some news, guys.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:11.434
A week after renaming
their company Meta,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.734
Facebook has learned

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:17.434
that there's already another
tech company called Meta

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:18.667
and they won't sell their name

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.234
for less than $20 million.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.868
When asked why they didn't do
their research, Facebook said,

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.634
"We did.
We just did it on Facebook."

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.734
Yep, the name Meta
is already being used.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.434
Facebook was like "Fine,
if that's taken,

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.000
we're just going to go
with our backup choice --

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.100
TikTok."

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.934
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.334
Speaking of social media,
this week,

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.467
Jay-Z joined Instagram...

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.400
...racked up more
than a million followers,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.133
then deleted his account
a day later.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:48.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.467
He was like,
"I don't want to get hooked.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.801
It'll be like Etsy
all over again."

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.434
Yeah, after 24 hours,
Jay-Z said, "Sunsets, food,

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.467
people's kids, I'm good.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.167
I don't need to do this."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.400
Yep, all it took was a day
for Jay-Z to realize,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.400
"I'm a billionaire married
to Beyoncé.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.901
Who cares what anyone
else is doing?"

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.801
Some news from Washington --

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.367
the White House announced
that their deadline

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.968
for their workplace
vaccine mandate is January 4th.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.767
It's great timing --
make sure everyone is vaccinated

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:14.968
right after the holidays.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.033
Some more COVID news --
I heard that there's

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:21.400
a potentially faster-spreading
Delta variant moving

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.400
through the U.S.,
called Delta-Plus.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.267
[ Applause ]

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.467
It's basically the Delta
variant, but, if you get it,

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.300
you can also stream movies
and shows for $13 a month.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
Got to admit it's a good deal.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:39.601
-Extra leg room.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:43.901
Some big sports news --

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.534
Packers quarterback
Aaron Rodgers

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.400
has tested positive for COVID
and it turns out

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.267
he may have lied
about being vaccinated.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.434
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.601
Yep, he told reporters
he was immunized,

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.434
which some people
are saying is misleading,

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:56.801
but that's not the only
confusing statement

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.467
that he's made
about his vaccine status.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.634
For example, in one
press conference, he said...

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:04.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.167
-Wow.
-Yeah. In another press
conference, he said...

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:11.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.701
And, finally, he cleared
things up by saying...

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.267
Some business news --
I read that CVS wants

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.067
to start hiring doctors

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:29.701
so that they can become a major
healthcare service provider.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:30.834
Yeah, instead of an X-ray,

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.400
they'll just drag you
across the scanner

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.801
at the self-checkout machine.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.234
[ Laughter ]
Boop!

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.067
Sorry, it didn't go through.
Get over here!

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.300
[ Laughter ]
-Beep!

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.767
-That's right,
CVS wants to hire doctors.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.601
It's kind of interesting,
but, even more interesting

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.234
are the questions
on the application

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.767
to become a CVS doctor.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.601
I'll show you what I mean.
First up, there's...

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
Then there's...

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
Next up, there's...

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
And, finally, there's...

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:09.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
Oh, that's --
-Whoa!

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:10.934
I never thought about that.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.234
Thank you.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.701
Some more business news --
this weekend,

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:19.067
UPS is looking to hire more
than 60,000 employees

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.033
at its annual
Brown Friday event.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.767
-[ Snickers ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.300
-And, of course --

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.734
And of course,
they won't hire anyone

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.400
because nobody will attend
an event called Brown Friday.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.067
Here's how the UPS event works.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:37.200
It starts on Friday, but,
if you show up three days late,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.267
the job is yours.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:43.167
Hey, guys, today, Starbucks
debuted their festive new drink,

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:46.234
called the Iced Sugar Cookie
Almond Milk Latte.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.701
[ Audience oohs ]
But they're not the only ones

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:48.701
getting into the holiday spirit.

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:49.767
Check out this new ad I just saw

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.300
from Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.767
-[ Boston accent ]
We here at Dunkin'
are serving up

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.701
some wicked awesome
new holiday drinks.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.100
So come on down and get
something for your kid brother.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.100
Like our new...

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.601
[ Laughter ]
Or how about a piping hot...

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:06.000
[ Audience ohs ]
Or maybe try our new...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.100
It's just a Styrofoam cup
filled with Sam Adams,

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.601
[ Laughter ]
so you can drink it
on the tee.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:11.868
From Dunkin'.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:16.634
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:20.934
-Hey, get this -- I saw that

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:23.067
